  "reasoning": "The claim states that lakes in Menindee County are located near a town on the banks of 'nagar.' The passages make clear that the Menindee Lakes are near the town of Menindee, which is on the banks of the Darling River. There is no mention of any town located on the banks of 'nagar,' nor is there any location or reference that matches 'nagar.' The claim appears to be a corruption or misreading of 'Darling' (perhaps 'Darling' → 'nagar'), but as stated, 'nagar' does not correspond to any real place mentioned in the passages. Therefore, the claim is not supported by the passages.",
  "summary": "The claim is not supported. The Menindee Lakes are located near the town of Menindee, which sits on the banks of the Darling River—not on the banks of 'nagar,' a place not referenced anywhere in the provided passages."
